/*
:name: store_unknown_field
:type: error
:error: names unknown field .z.
*/

// A whole-tuple assignment may only re-bind fields the destination already
// has. `z` is not part of `Point`, so the store is a compile error.
//
// The diagnostic comes from the detuple front end, which owns the shape once a
// named tuple type is split into per-field leaves. It used to come from
// upass.typecheck here and ONLY here, because a type whose fields carry
// DEFAULTS failed to split at all (2f-defaulted_tuple) -- the byte-equivalent
// `type Point = (x:u8, y:u8)` already reported the message below. Now that
// defaulted and plain types split alike, both spellings report identically.

type Point = (x:u8 = nil, y:u8 = nil)
mut t:Point = (x=1, y=2)
t = (y=5, z=9) // locate_error_here
